-- הסכם אופק חדש (25.12.2008), §49: the conversion of a primary-school
-- teacher on the junior-high base of 24 weekly hours — in grades 7–9, and
-- in grades 1–6 where the base was kept — is a junior-high teacher's, with
-- Y "greater by 12.5%" than §44's; one on both bases, a weighted Y; and the
-- clause's example.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `base-agreement-common`
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `base-agreement-44`
§ `49`

-- akn:art_49 The clause's heading line: the conversion of teachers in a primary school on the junior-high base, a special-education one included.

-- (א)–(ב): the junior-high conversion, its Y "יהיה גדול ב -12.5% מהתוספת
-- הקבועה בסעיף 44". F-ofek-hadash-base-49-a: the clause's own example
-- ((ג) ¶3) adds 12.5 points (27 + 12.5); convention amounts.increase would
-- multiply (27 × 1.125). The example decides the reading here: an
-- exception to the convention, recorded there.
@ref akn:art_49__para_a akn:art_49__para_b
GIVEN s IS A `status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Y on the 24-hour base in a primary school` s IS
    `Y on a single base` s `the junior-high base of 24 weekly hours` PLUS 12.5

-- (ג): on both bases, the weighted Y of §44, the 24-hour share with the
-- raised Y.
@ref akn:art_49__para_c
GIVEN s IS A `status`, `position on the 24-hour base` IS A NUMBER, `position on the 30-hour base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Y on both bases in a primary school` s `position on the 24-hour base` `position on the 30-hour base` IS
    (    `position on the 24-hour base` TIMES `Y on the 24-hour base in a primary school` s
     PLUS `position on the 30-hour base` TIMES `Y on a single base` s `the primary base of 30 weekly hours`)
    DIVIDED BY (`position on the 24-hour base` PLUS `position on the 30-hour base`)

-- The example (¶2–¶4): a regular teacher, 70% in grades 1–6 and 40% in
-- grades 7–9, 110% in all: (70/110 × 117%) + (40/110 × 139.5%), printed as
-- Y = 25.18.
@ref akn:art_49__para_c/p2 akn:art_49__para_c/p3 akn:art_49__para_c/p4
#ASSERT `to the agora` (`Y on both bases in a primary school` `a regular teacher` 0.4 0.7) EQUALS 25.18

-- F-ofek-hadash-base-49-a's evidence: the convention's reading misses the
-- example's 25.18.
`Y by convention amounts.increase` MEANS
    (0.4 TIMES (27 TIMES 1.125) PLUS 0.7 TIMES 17) DIVIDED BY 1.1
`the example adds points, not a share` MEANS
    NOT (`to the agora` `Y by convention amounts.increase` EQUALS 25.18)
#ASSERT `the example adds points, not a share`
